# Deck CODEOWNERS
#
# GitHub requests review from these owners for pull requests that touch
# the matched paths. Update this file after running /uw-slides:plan-deck
# to reflect who owns which slides.
#
# Pattern: each slides/<id>.md maps to the person responsible for that slide's
# content — the "owner:" field in the brief's front matter. GitHub CODEOWNERS
# uses the last matching rule, so slide-specific lines below override the
# default.
#
# Syntax: <path-pattern>  @github-username
#
# Example after planning a deck with four owners:
#
#   slides/                       @project-lead        # fallback for unlisted slides
#   slides/01-title.md            @project-lead
#   slides/02-land-ack.md         @project-lead
#   slides/03-overview.md         @presenter-a
#   slides/04-methods.md          @presenter-b
#   slides/05-results.md          @presenter-b
#   slides/06-discussion.md       @presenter-a
#   slides/07-next-steps.md       @project-lead
#   slides/08-closing.md          @project-lead
#
# Generated fragments (content/) are not listed: they are owned by whoever
# owns the brief they were generated from, and reviews are done through the
# brief, not the HTML.

# Default: all slides go to the deck owner until specific owners are assigned
slides/                             @change-me
